# Clean, readable controller integration tests

When writing or updating `@WebMvcTest` / web-slice tests, prioritize clarity and match existing test structure in the module.

## Prefer DTOs over raw JSON strings

Serialize generated/command models with `JsonMapper` — do not hand-write JSON bodies.

```text
❌ .content("{\"isPublic\":true}")
✅ .content(jsonMapper.writeValueAsString(UploadToStorageCommand.builder().isPublic(true).build()))
```

## Parameterize shared scenarios

Use `@ParameterizedTest(name = "{0}")` with `@CsvSource` or `@MethodSource` when cases share the same flow and differ only by inputs/expectations (missing resource across GET/PUT, public vs private key prefix, bad-key across endpoints).

Keep distinct business flows as separate `@Test` methods when parameterization would obscure the scenario.

## Match sibling test structure

Copy the nearest controller integration test in the same area:

- `@WebMvcTest(controllers = …)` + `@Import({ GlobalExceptionHandler, *ServiceImpl, SecurityConfig, … })`
- Real service; `@MockitoBean` only repos/ports
- `@DisplayName` on class and methods; method names `action_scenario_expectedHttp`
- Fixtures in `modules/<module>/support/*Fixtures.java`
- Auth helpers (`jwt()`, `adminJwt()`) as peers do

## Also follow

`test-service-behavior-only` — test service rules, not framework validation.

# Test service behavior, not framework code

Web-slice / controller integration tests must exercise **application/service rules**, not Spring MVC, Bean Validation, Jackson, or other library behavior.

## Do test

- Happy paths through controller → real service → mocked repos/caches
- Domain/business outcomes: not found, conflict, reactivate, soft-delete, denormalized fields, role updates
- Error codes/messages produced by our `BusinessException` hierarchy

## Do not test

- Request body validation (`@NotNull`, `@Size`, blank fields, missing required JSON)
- Path/query binding (invalid UUID, type mismatch)
- Filter/pagination constraint validation (`size` min/max, sort patterns)
- Malformed JSON / media type handling
- Anything whose failure mode is entirely Spring or Jakarta Validation

```text
❌ createClassroom_missingName_returns400
❌ getClassroomById_invalidUuid_returns400
❌ getAllClassrooms_invalidSize_returns400
❌ createClassroomMember_invalidBody_returns400

✅ creates a classroom
✅ fails to get a classroom that does not exist
✅ rejects creating a member that is already active
✅ reactivates a previously removed classroom member
```

If a case only fails because the framework rejected the request before the service ran, omit it.